--> A tuple is used to store multiple values of different data types in a single variable.
-->Tuples are useful when a function needs to return multiple related values.
For example, a student has:
- Name – String
- Age – Int
- Mark – Double
Instead of creating three separate variables, we can use a tuple.

Creating a tuple
---------------
var student = ("Dhanush", 21, 85.5)
print(student)---->("Dhanush", 21, 85.5)

Access tuple values
-------------------
->We can access tuple values using index numbers.
->Tuple indexing starts from 0.
var student = ("Dhanush", 21, 85.5)
print(student.0)---->Dhanush
print(student.1)---->21
print(student.2)---->85.5

Named tuples
------------
->We can give names to each value.
var student = (
    name: "Dhanush",
    age: 21,
    mark: 85.5
)
print(student.name)---->Dhanush
print(student.age)----->21
print(student.mark)---->85.5

Tuple in a function
-------------------
func getStudent() -> (String, Int) {
    return ("Dhanush", 21)
}
let result = getStudent()
print(result.0)---->Dhanush
print(result.1)---->21
